WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:09.153
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit thirteen: Present Perfect (introduction). Today you will talk about experiences and recent results.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.680
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:22.773
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.386
Have.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:28.393
Have means the helping verb for I, you, we and they.

8
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:30.101
I have finished.

9
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.835
Your turn. Say: Have.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.492
Have.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.216
Has.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:42.029
Has means the helping verb for he, she and it.

13
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:43.827
She has arrived.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.802
Your turn. Say: Has.

15
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.586
Has.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.049
Ever.

17
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.061
Ever means at any time in your life.

18
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.208
Have you ever been to Japan?

19
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.086
Your turn. Say: Ever.

20
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:03.737
Ever.

21
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:05.299
Never.

22
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:08.132
Never means not at any time.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.310
I have never eaten sushi.

24
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.197
Your turn. Say: Never.

25
00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:16.988
Never.

26
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.751
Already.

27
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.469
Already means before now, sooner than expected.

28
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.549
I have already eaten.

29
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.628
Your turn. Say: Already.

30
00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:31.468
Already.

31
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:32.858
Yet.

32
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.394
Yet means up to now, used in questions and negatives.

33
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:39.368
Have you finished yet?

34
00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:42.357
Your turn. Say: Yet.

35
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:45.934
Yet.

36
00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:47.940
Experience.

37
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.203
Experience means something that you have done or lived through.

38
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:54.793
Travelling is a great experience.

39
00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:58.512
Your turn. Say: Experience.

40
00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:02.693
Experience.

41
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.707
Past participle.

42
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:08.541
Past participle means the third form of a verb.

43
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.509
Eaten is the past participle of eat.

44
00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:15.117
Your turn. Say: Past participle.

45
00:02:17.967 --> 00:02:19.362
Past participle.

46
00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.725
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.117
Visal, have you ever been to Siem Reap?

48
00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:40.441
Yes, I have. I have visited it twice. The present perfect is have or has + the past participle. We use it for life experience and for past actions that matter now.

49
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.039
What are ever and never?

50
00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:56.432
Ever is for questions: Have you ever tried durian? Never is a negative: I have never tried it. Already and yet show timing: I have already finished. Have you finished yet?

51
00:02:57.517 --> 00:02:59.330
What is a past participle?

52
00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:13.764
Regular verbs end in -ed, like visited. Irregular verbs change: eat, eaten; see, seen; go, gone or been. We do not say when it happened, because the time is not important.

53
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.447
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:22.603
Grammar focus: Present perfect: have and has plus past participle.

55
00:03:22.903 --> 00:03:24.148
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.745
I have visited Siem Reap twice.

57
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:29.336
She has never eaten durian.

58
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.099
Have you ever been to Japan?

59
00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:42.225
Use have / has + past participle for experiences and for results now. Do not use finished time words like yesterday. Use ever, never, already and yet.

60
00:03:42.983 --> 00:03:46.425
Be careful! Don't say: I have seen him yesterday.

61
00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.773
Say: I saw him yesterday.

62
00:03:51.073 --> 00:03:53.409
Use past simple with yesterday.

63
00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.026
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.833 --> 00:03:59.485
Life Experiences.

65
00:03:59.785 --> 00:04:03.061
I have visited Siem Reap twice, but I have never been to Japan.

66
00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.507
My sister has already finished her homework.

67
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.139
Have you ever tried durian? It is a strange experience.

68
00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.587
They haven't arrived yet.

69
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.226
The past participle of go can be gone or been.

70
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:22.370
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:23.217 --> 00:04:25.019
I blank never eaten sushi.

72
00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:28.496
A, have. B, has. C, am.

73
00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:33.661
The answer is A: have.

74
00:04:34.817 --> 00:04:36.526
She blank already finished.

75
00:04:36.826 --> 00:04:39.818
A, have. B, has. C, had.

76
00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.471
The answer is B: has.

77
00:04:46.617 --> 00:04:48.221
Have you blank been to Thailand?

78
00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.513
A, ever. B, yet. C, never.

79
00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.602
The answer is A: ever.

80
00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.599
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:04.353
A, I have seen him yesterday.. B, I have seen him.. C, I have saw him..

82
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.225
The answer is B: I have seen him..

83
00:05:11.383 --> 00:05:14.521
According to the reading, what has the sister already finished?

84
00:05:14.821 --> 00:05:18.521
A, her homework. B, her dinner. C, her test.

85
00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.600
The answer is A: her homework.

86
00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.789
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:32.172
Write a sentence about something you have never done.

88
00:05:40.983 --> 00:05:42.878
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.178 --> 00:05:55.539
I have never ridden a horse. I have seen horses in pictures, but I haven't tried it. I use have never + past participle to talk about something I have not done in my life.

90
00:05:55.839 --> 00:05:57.560
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:04.400
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect: have and has plus past participle.

92
00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.722
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:06:09.022 --> 00:06:11.721
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:12.021 --> 00:06:14.952
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

